# Trunk-based development

`main` is the only long-lived branch and stays releasable.

- Branch from latest `main`. Keep the branch short-lived. Open a PR. Squash-merge. GitHub deletes the branch.
- Never push to `main`, force-push `main`, or create long-lived branches (`develop`, `release/*`, `hotfix/*`).
- One concern per PR. Name branches `type/short-description` (`feat/plugin-manifest`, `fix/ci-gate`).
- Merge requires 1 approving review, resolved conversations, and the `CI` check green. Admins may bypass on a PR for emergencies only.
- Add new CI jobs as `needs` of the `CI` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Do not add extra required checks to the ruleset.
